{"ref":"BDB, עַלְמָה","hw":"עַלְמָה","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">עַלְמָה</span></big>  <strong>n.f. young woman (</strong>ripe sexually; maid or newly married<strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 24:43\" href=\"/Genesis.24.43\">Gn 24:43</a> (J), <a data-ref=\"Exodus 2:8\" href=\"/Exodus.2.8\">Ex 2:8</a> (E), <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 30:19\" href=\"/Proverbs.30.19\">Pr 30:19</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 7:14\" href=\"/Isaiah.7.14\">Is 7:14</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲלָמוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 68:26\" href=\"/Psalms.68.26\">ψ 68:26</a> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 1:3\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.1.3\">Ct 1:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 6:8\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.6.8\">6:8</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל־עֲלָמוֹת</span> <em>to</em> (the voice of) <em>young women</em>, either lit., or of soprano or falsetto of boys: <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 15:20\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.15.20\">1 Ch 15:20</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 9:1\" href=\"/Psalms.9.1\">ψ 9:1</a> (read <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל־עֲלָמוֹת לַבֵּן</span> [for <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל־מוּת לַבֵּן</span>, ‘<em>voce virginea a pueris</em> decantandum,’ Thes), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 46:1\" href=\"/Psalms.46.1\">46:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 48:15\" href=\"/Psalms.48.15\">48:15</a> (read <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל־עֲלָמוֹת</span> [for <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל־מוּת</span>]; tr. prob. to <a data-ref=\"Psalms 49:1\" href=\"/Psalms.49.1\">49:1</a>).","next":"BDB, עֲלוּמִים","prev":"BDB, עֶ֫לֶם"}